0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Security adoption · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/#doc-2026-11-06-using-saf-effectively-03" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">SAF navigation now directs readers by objective and organizational role</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The retitled “Using SAF effectively” article replaces top-down, build-up, and scenario-driven patterns with tables that route readers to strategy, architecture, disciplines, scenarios, technologies, workshops, and related guidance based on their objectives or roles.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.security.admin.news/day/2026-11-06/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 6 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
